  <!-- ── SLIDE 8: RETRIEVAL & RECENCY ── -->
  <div class="slide" id="slide-8">
    <div class="label">07 — Retrieval</div>
    <div class="section-title">
      <div class="num">07</div>
      <h2>Retrieval Strategy & Recency</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-2" style="flex:1; gap:32px;">
      <div>
        <h3>LightRAG — Why It Fits</h3>
        <ul class="styled" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
          <li><strong>MongoDB native</strong> backend support</li>
          <li><strong>Dual-mode retrieval</strong> — vector similarity + graph traversal together</li>
          <li><strong>Local mode</strong> — specific entity lookup (AppID, PageID, RowType)</li>
          <li><strong>Global mode</strong> — community summaries across a sector</li>
          <li><strong>Open source</strong>, self-hostable, fits your stack</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Paragraph Classification</h3>
        <table class="tbl">
          <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th><th>Graph</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><span class="tag green">CONTEXTUAL</span></td><td>Annotates nearby table</td><td>Linked to PageID + RowType</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="tag amber">STANDALONE</span></td><td>Meeting notes, commentary</td><td>PageID only, semantic search</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Recency-Weighted Scoring</h3>
        <div class="code"><span class="c">// Re-rank after vector retrieval</span>
<span class="k">final_score</span> = semantic_score × recency_weight(pageDate)

<span class="c">// Weight schedule (per sector)</span>
<span class="k">current year</span>  → <span class="v">1.00</span>
<span class="k">-1 year</span>       → <span class="v">0.85</span>
<span class="k">-2 years</span>      → <span class="v">0.70</span>
<span class="k">-3 years</span>      → <span class="v">0.55</span>
<span class="k">floor</span>         → <span class="v">0.40</span>  <span class="c">(oldest pages not excluded)</span></div>
        <div style="margin-top:16px;" class="callout">
          <strong>Scope recency per sector.</strong> A 2021 page in Sector A is not comparable to a 2021 page in Sector B if they evolve at different rates. <code style="color:var(--accent)">pageDate</code> is indexed DESC on the edge collection for zero-cost sorting.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── SLIDE 9: ADK AGENT ── -->
  <div class="slide" id="slide-9">
    <div class="label">08 — Agent Layer</div>
    <div class="section-title">
      <div class="num">08</div>
      <h2>Google ADK Agent Tools</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-2" style="flex:1; gap:32px;">
      <div>
        <h3>Tool Signatures</h3>
        <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:12px;">
          <h4>search_graph(sector, query, filters?)</h4>
          <p>Atlas Vector Search + graph traversal. Applies recency re-ranking. Sector always resolved first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card amber" style="margin-bottom:12px;">
          <h4>get_app_pages(appId, sector?)</h4>
          <p>Which pages reference this app, newest first? Single edge query with DESC sort.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card purple" style="margin-bottom:12px;">
          <h4>get_page_context(pageId)</h4>
          <p>Page metadata + all rows, paragraphs, and file statuses.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card green">
          <h4>get_rowtype_summary(canonicalType, sector?)</h4>
          <p>All apps affected by this row type. Two-hop: RowType → Rows → Files → Apps.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Query Pattern — get_app_pages</h3>
        <div class="code"><span class="c">// "Which pages reference APP_XYZ, newest first?"</span>
edges.<span class="k">find</span>({
  <span class="n">"to.id"</span>: <span class="s">"APP_XYZ001"</span>,
  <span class="n">"relationship"</span>: <span class="s">"LISTS_APP"</span>,
  <span class="n">"context.sector"</span>: <span class="s">"SECTOR_A"</span>
}).<span class="k">sort</span>({ <span class="n">"context.pageDate"</span>: <span class="v">-1</span> })</div>
        <div style="margin-top:16px;">
          <h3>Query Pattern — get_rowtype_summary</h3>
          <div class="code"><span class="c">// Step 1: rows of this type</span>
edges.<span class="k">find</span>({ <span class="n">"to.id"</span>: canonicalType,
  <span class="n">"relationship"</span>: <span class="s">"HAS_ROWTYPE"</span> })
→ collect rowIds

<span class="c">// Step 2: files from those rows</span>
edges.<span class="k">find</span>({ <span class="n">"from.id"</span>: { <span class="k">$in</span>: rowIds },
  <span class="n">"relationship"</span>: <span class="s">"REFERENCES_FILE"</span> })
→ collect fileIds

<span class="c">// Step 3: apps from those files</span>
edges.<span class="k">find</span>({ <span class="n">"from.id"</span>: { <span class="k">$in</span>: fileIds },
  <span class="n">"relationship"</span>: <span class="s">"LISTS_APP"</span> })</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── SLIDE 10: RISKS ── -->
