          <tr>
            <td>OCR quality on images</td>
            <td><span class="tag red">High</span></td>
            <td>Confidence threshold gate. Below threshold → discard extraction, flag file. Confidence stored on edge metadata.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>PPT files with mostly images</td>
            <td><span class="tag amber">Medium</span></td>
            <td>Fallback to slide title + speaker notes only. Mark parse status as PARTIAL.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>RowType clustering drift over time</td>
            <td><span class="tag amber">Medium</span></td>
            <td>Versioned canonical type registry. Re-run normalizer when new variants appear. Never auto-merge without review.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Same AppID, different sectors</td>
            <td><span class="tag green">Low</span></td>
            <td>AppID is globally unique — confirmed. App node is singleton. Sector lives on edge context only.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Multi-hop traversal performance</td>
            <td><span class="tag amber">Medium</span></td>
            <td>Compound indexes on edges collection with sector + pageDate. Derived <code>APPEARS_IN_SECTOR</code> edge computed post-ingestion for shortcut queries.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div style="margin-top:20px;" class="callout amber">
        <strong>Derived edge:</strong> <code>App ──[APPEARS_IN_SECTOR]──▶ Sector</code> computed after full sector ingestion. Enables fast "all apps in Sector X" without full traversal.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

